From 5871dbca93d3a6e50d445357f0e423845b08f794 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cole Morgan <colerussellmorgan@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:42:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] KOReaderSync: route sync requests through a transport
 seam

KOReaderSyncClient keeps building requests and parsing responses, but
hands each request to a KOSyncTransport. The default transport is the
existing Wi-Fi HTTPS client with unchanged headers and status handling;
setTransport() lets a caller substitute another link. The TLS heap
preflight only runs for transports that open TLS on the device.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
